{
  "version": 1,
  "default": "cc-dark",
  "_comment": [
    "Themes are DATA. Adding one is an edit to this file - no CSS and no JS change.",
    "A theme's tokens are written onto document.documentElement.style at runtime, so",
    "there is no stylesheet swap and no flash of unstyled content.",
    "",
    "Every theme MUST define the full token set below; the frontend does not merge",
    "against a base, because a half-defined theme that silently inherits is worse to",
    "debug than one that fails visibly.",
    "",
    "Brand note: orange is an ACCENT, never a fill. It marks the active nav item, the",
    "focus ring, key values and 1px rules. Filling panels with it would read as a",
    "warning state, which is exactly what --warn is for.",
    "",
    "Surface contract: --bg is the canvas; --panel and --panel-2 are legacy surfaces.",
    "--surface-1 and --surface-2 are increasing elevations; borders have subtle/strong weights.",
    "--ok mirrors legacy --safe. Semantic colours and --series-1..6 support status and charts.",
    "All foreground tokens are checked at >=4.5:1 on every surface; high-contrast >=7:1.",
    "Series distinguish categories, not status; always pair colour with labels or markers."
  ],
  "tokens": [
    "--bg",
    "--panel",
    "--panel-2",
    "--line",
    "--text",
    "--muted",
    "--accent",
    "--accent-dim",
    "--safe",
    "--warn",
    "--danger",
    "--ok",
    "--info",
    "--surface-1",
    "--surface-2",
    "--border-subtle",
    "--border-strong",
    "--series-1",
    "--series-2",
    "--series-3",
    "--series-4",
    "--series-5",
    "--series-6"
  ],
